grep -i -A20 "^E:.*$name" r_info.txt | less

But if you want to write something non trivial - both in terms of usefulness
and programming - write a virtual character equipment simulator. Parse a
character dump and let the user enter a set of attributes (resistance, tele
and such). Now calculate the set of equipment fitting those attributes.
Icing on the cake, let the user prioritize the attributes and let him mark
equipment positions as 'fixed' (don't consider). Provide a nice, graphical
interface with point & click.
Not really needed for single-dungeon variants, but very nice for Tome and
Hengband. And it'd quieten the 'can be done with a shell script' crowd
instantly:)

